INFO:agent.loop:\u26a1 Executing tool: 'knowledge_agent' with arguments: {"source_title": "Public attribution and laundering analyses for Ronin and Harmony Horizon thefts", "source_url": "SRC-001; SRC-002; SRC-003", "text": "SRC-001 (Elliptic, May 9 2023) reports FBI confirmation that North Korea-backed Lazarus Group was behind the June 24, 2022 Harmony Horizon Bridge hack, which stole $99.7M. Elliptic says its prior attribution was based on similarities to Lazarus blockchain laundering patterns. It reports Harmony funds were programmatically structured through Tornado Cash, mirroring laundering used after Ronin. Elliptic estimates more than $555M from the two hacks went through Tornado Cash: >$468M Ronin and $96M Harmony. After sanctions, Lazarus structured Harmony funds through Railgun; Elliptic estimated ~70% of ETH sent through Railgun was Harmony-related, then funds were deposited into Binance, Huobi, and other exchanges; Binance and Huobi announced blocking/seizing portions. SRC-002 (Chainalysis, Sep 8 2022) reports North Korea-linked groups, especially Lazarus, were associated with about $1B stolen from DeFi in 2022. For Ronin, attackers accessed five of nine validator private keys, withdrew 173,600 ETH and 25.5M USDC, and used >12,000 addresses. It describes a five-stage North Korea laundering pattern: intermediary wallets; batch Tornado Cash mixing; ETH-to-BTC swaps; batch Bitcoin mixing; deposits to crypto-to-fiat services. It also reports chain-hopping: ETH bridged Ethereum to BNB, swapped to USDD, bridged to BitTorrent, with hundreds of similar transactions. More than $30M was seized, about 10% of total at then-values. SRC-003 (Elliptic, Mar 29 2022, updated for Apr 14 sanctions) reports Ronin theft six days earlier: 173,600 ETH and 25.5M USDC, valued $540M then; OFAC listed the thief Ethereum address owner as Lazarus Group, a North Korean state hacking group. It reports social engineering assessment, DEX swaps of USDC to ETH, $16.7M ETH through three centralized exchanges, then $80.3M through Tornado Cash; $9.7M in intermediary wallets and $433M remaining in original wallet at that time. Elliptic assessed similarities to prior Lazarus attacks in victim location, social-engineering method, and laundering pattern. Sources do not establish that APT38 is an alias for Lazarus or provide specific wallet addresses beyond describing a Ronin thief Ethereum address; do not infer that equivalence."}
